{"id":"mahabharata-6-062","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":62,"title":"द्विषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 62 · Narayana, Nara and the birth of Krishna","summary":{"en":"Bhishma tells how Brahma sought the supreme lord, who promised to take birth among men as Nara and Narayana. He warns Duryodhana that Krishna and Arjuna are those ancient sages and cannot be defeated.","kn":"ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನು ಪರಮೇಶ್ವರನನ್ನು ಬೇಡಿದ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನೂ, ಅವನು ನರ-ನಾರಾಯಣರಾಗಿ ಮನುಷ್ಯರಲ್ಲಿ ಹುಟ್ಟುವೆನೆಂದು ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡಿದುದನ್ನೂ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೃಷ್ಣ-ಅರ್ಜುನರೇ ಆ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಋಷಿಗಳು, ಅವರನ್ನು ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾಗದು ಎಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म बताते हैं कि ब्रह्मा ने परमेश्वर से प्रार्थना की और उन्होंने नर-नारायण रूप में मनुष्यों में जन्म लेने का वचन दिया। वे दुर्योधन को चेताते हैं कि कृष्ण और अर्जुन वही प्राचीन ऋषि हैं, अजेय।","te":"బ్రహ్మ పరమేశ్వరుని ప్రార్థించగా ఆయన నర నారాయణులుగా మనుషులలో పుడతానని మాటిచ్చిన కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. కృష్ణార్జునులే ఆ ప్రాచీన ఋషులని, వారిని జయించలేరని దుర్యోధనుని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பிரம்மன் பரமேசுவரனை வேண்ட, அவர் நர நாராயணராக மனிதரிடையே பிறப்பதாக வாக்களித்த கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். கண்ணனும் அர்ஜுனனுமே அந்தப் பழைய முனிவர்கள், அவர்களை வெல்ல முடியாது என்று துரியோதனனை எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"പരമേശ്വരനെ കാണാൻ ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അന്വേഷിച്ചതും, അദ്ദേഹം നര-നാരായണന്മാരായി മനുഷ്യരിൽ ജനിക്കാമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്തതും ഭീഷ്മർ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണനും അർജുനനും ആ പുരാതന ഋഷിമാരാണെന്നും അവരെ തോൽപ്പിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം ദുര്യോധനന് മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.62; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः स भगवान्देवो लोकानां परमेश्वरः ।\nब्रह्माणं प्रत्युवाचेदं स्निग्धगम्भीरया गिरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the blessed god, supreme Lord of the worlds, answered Brahma in a gentle, deep voice."}},{"n":2,"text":"विदितं तात योगान्मे सर्वमेतत्तवेप्सितम् ।\nतथा तद्भवितेत्युक्त्वा तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I know through yoga, my dear, all that you desire. So be it.\" Saying this, he vanished on the spot."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो देवर्षिगन्धर्वा विस्मयं परमं गताः ।\nकौतूहलपराः सर्वे पितामहमथाब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the divine sages and gandharvas, filled with great wonder and curiosity, all spoke to the grandfather."}},{"n":4,"text":"को न्वयं यो भगवता प्रणम्य विनयाद्विभो ।\nवाग्भिः स्तुतो वरिष्ठाभिः श्रोतुमिच्छाम तं वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who is this, lord, whom you bowed to humbly and praised in such excellent words? We wish to hear.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु भगवान्प्रत्युवाच पितामहः ।\nदेवब्रह्मर्षिगन्धर्वान्सर्वान्मधुरया गिरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the blessed grandfather answered all the gods, brahmin sages and gandharvas in a sweet voice."}},{"n":6,"text":"यत्तत्परं भविष्यं च भवितव्यं च यत्परम् ।\nभूतात्मा यः प्रभुश्चैव ब्रह्म यच्च परं पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who is the highest, the future and what is to be, the self of beings, the Lord, the Brahman and the supreme state,"}},{"n":7,"text":"तेनास्मि कृतसंवादः प्रसन्नेन सुरर्षभाः ।\nजगतोऽनुग्रहार्थाय याचितो मे जगत्पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with him, gods and bulls, I have just conversed, and he is pleased. I begged the lord of the world for the world's benefit:"}},{"n":8,"text":"मानुषं लोकमातिष्ठ वासुदेव इति श्रुतः ।\nअसुराणां वधार्थाय संभवस्व महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Take on the world of men, known as Vasudeva; be born on the surface of the earth to kill the asuras.'"}},{"n":9,"text":"संग्रामे निहता ये ते दैत्यदानवराक्षसाः ।\nत इमे नृषु संभूता घोररूपा महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those Daityas, Danavas and rakshasas who were killed in battle have now been born among men, of terrible form and great strength."}},{"n":10,"text":"तेषां वधार्थं भगवान्नरेण सहितो वशी ।\nमानुषीं योनिमास्थाय चरिष्यति महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"To kill them the blessed, self-controlled Lord, together with Nara, will take a human birth and move about on earth."}},{"n":11,"text":"नरनारायणौ यौ तौ पुराणावृषिसत्तमौ ।\nसहितौ मानुषे लोके संभूतावमितद्युती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two ancient best of sages, Nara and Narayana, of boundless splendor, have been born together in the world of men."}},{"n":12,"text":"अजेयौ समरे यत्तौ सहितावमरैरपि ।\nमूढास्त्वेतौ न जानन्ति नरनारायणावृषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intent in battle, they are unconquerable even by the immortals together; but fools do not know these two sages as Nara and Narayana."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्याहमात्मजो ब्रह्मा सर्वस्य जगतः पतिः ।\nवासुदेवोऽर्चनीयो वः सर्वलोकमहेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am his son, Brahma, and he is the lord of the whole world. Vasudeva, great Lord of all worlds, is to be worshipped by you."}},{"n":14,"text":"तथा मनुष्योऽयमिति कदाचित्सुरसत्तमाः ।\nनावज्ञेयो महावीर्यः शङ्खचक्रगदाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So never, best of gods, should the mighty one who bears the conch, discus and mace be despised as 'just a man.'"}},{"n":15,"text":"एतत्परमकं गुह्यमेतत्परमकं पदम् ।\nएतत्परमकं ब्रह्म एतत्परमकं यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the supreme secret, this is the supreme state, this is the supreme Brahman, this is the supreme glory."}},{"n":16,"text":"एतदक्षरमव्यक्तमेतत्तच्छाश्वतं महत् ।\nएतत्पुरुषसंज्ञं वै गीयते ज्ञायते न च ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the imperishable and unmanifest, this is the eternal and great; this is called the Purusha; he is sung of, but not known."}},{"n":17,"text":"एतत्परमकं तेज एतत्परमकं सुखम् ।\nएतत्परमकं सत्यं कीर्तितं विश्वकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the supreme light, the supreme happiness, the supreme truth, as the maker of all has proclaimed."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मात्सर्वैः सुरैः सेन्द्रैर्लोकैश्चामितविक्रमः ।\nनावज्ञेयो वासुदेवो मानुषोऽयमिति प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore Vasudeva, the Lord of boundless prowess, is not to be despised by any gods with Indra or by the worlds as 'only a man.'"}},{"n":19,"text":"यश्च मानुषमात्रोऽयमिति ब्रूयात्सुमन्दधीः ।\nहृषीकेशमवज्ञानात्तमाहुः पुरुषाधमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, of very dull mind, says 'he is only a man,' despising Hrishikesha, they call the lowest of men."}},{"n":20,"text":"योगिनं तं महात्मानं प्रविष्टं मानुषीं तनुम् ।\nअवमन्येद्वासुदेवं तमाहुस्तामसं जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call a man of tamas the one who scorns Vasudeva, the great-souled yogi who has entered a human body."}},{"n":21,"text":"देवं चराचरात्मानं श्रीवत्साङ्कं सुवर्चसम् ।\nपद्मनाभं न जानाति तमाहुस्तामसं जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who does not know the god, self of the moving and unmoving, marked with the Shrivatsa, of fine radiance, the lotus-navel, they call a man of tamas."}},{"n":22,"text":"किरीटकौस्तुभधरं मित्राणामभयंकरम् ।\nअवजानन्महात्मानं घोरे तमसि मज्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who disregards the great-souled one who wears the crown and the Kaustubha, who gives his friends freedom from fear, sinks into dreadful darkness."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवं विदित्वा तत्त्वार्थं लोकानामीश्वरेश्वरः ।\nवासुदेवो नमस्कार्यः सर्वलोकैः सुरोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the truth thus, best of gods, Vasudeva, the Lord of the lords of the worlds, is to be bowed to by all the worlds.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा स भगवान्सर्वान्देवगणान्पुरा ।\nविसृज्य सर्वलोकात्मा जगाम भवनं स्वकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus to all the hosts of gods, the blessed one, self of all the worlds, dismissed them and went to his own abode."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततो देवाः सगन्धर्वा मुनयोऽप्सरसोऽपि च ।\nकथां तां ब्रह्मणा गीतां श्रुत्वा प्रीता दिवं ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the gods with gandharvas, the sages and the apsarases, delighted at hearing the story sung by Brahma, went to heaven."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतच्छ्रुतं मया तात ऋषीणां भावितात्मनाम् ।\nवासुदेवं कथयतां समवाये पुरातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This I heard, my dear, from sages of purified souls, speaking of Vasudeva in an assembly, in ancient times."}},{"n":27,"text":"जामदग्न्यस्य रामस्य मार्कण्डेयस्य धीमतः ।\nव्यासनारदयोश्चापि श्रुतं श्रुतविशारद ॥","meaning":{"en":"I heard it also from Rama son of Jamadagni, from wise Markandeya, and from Vyasa and Narada, you who are learned in what is heard."}},{"n":28,"text":"एतमर्थं च विज्ञाय श्रुत्वा च प्रभुमव्ययम् ।\nवासुदेवं महात्मानं लोकानामीश्वरेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this meaning and having heard of the imperishable Lord, the great-souled Vasudeva, Lord of the lords of the worlds,"}},{"n":29,"text":"यस्यासावात्मजो ब्रह्मा सर्वस्य जगतः पिता ।\nकथं न वासुदेवोऽयमर्च्यश्चेज्यश्च मानवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"whose son is Brahma, father of the whole world: how should this Vasudeva not be revered and worshipped by men?"}},{"n":30,"text":"वारितोऽसि पुरा तात मुनिभिर्वेदपारगैः ।\nमा गच्छ संयुगं तेन वासुदेवेन धीमता ।\nमा पाण्डवैः सार्धमिति तच्च मोहान्न बुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, my dear, you were warned by sages who had mastered the Vedas: \"Do not go to battle with that wise Vasudeva, and not with the Pandavas.\" Yet from delusion you do not understand it."}},{"n":31,"text":"मन्ये त्वां राक्षसं क्रूरं तथा चासि तमोवृतः ।\nयस्माद्द्विषसि गोविन्दं पाण्डवं च धनंजयम् ।\nनरनारायणौ देवौ नान्यो द्विष्याद्धि मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think you are a cruel rakshasa, enveloped in tamas, since you hate Govinda and the Pandava Dhananjaya. No other man would hate the gods Nara and Narayana."}},{"n":32,"text":"तस्माद्ब्रवीमि ते राजन्नेष वै शाश्वतोऽव्ययः ।\nसर्वलोकमयो नित्यः शास्ता धाता धरो ध्रुवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore I tell you, king, he is eternal and imperishable, made of all the worlds, ever the ruler, supporter, bearer and fixed one."}},{"n":33,"text":"लोकान्धारयते यस्त्रींश्चराचरगुरुः प्रभुः ।\nयोद्धा जयश्च जेता च सर्वप्रकृतिरीश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He upholds the three worlds, the Lord, the teacher of the moving and unmoving, the fighter, victory and the victor, the nature of all, the Ruler."}},{"n":34,"text":"राजन्सत्त्वमयो ह्येष तमोरागविवर्जितः ।\nयतः कृष्णस्ततो धर्मो यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, he is made of sattva, free of tamas and rajas. Where Krishna is, there is dharma; where dharma is, there is victory."}},{"n":35,"text":"तस्य माहात्म्ययोगेन योगेनात्मन एव च ।\nधृताः पाण्डुसुता राजञ्जयश्चैषां भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the power of his greatness and by his own yoga, the sons of Pandu are upheld, king, and they will have victory."}},{"n":36,"text":"श्रेयोयुक्तां सदा बुद्धिं पाण्डवानां दधाति यः ।\nबलं चैव रणे नित्यं भयेभ्यश्चैव रक्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gives the Pandavas always a mind turned toward the good, and always protects their strength in battle and guards them from fears."}},{"n":37,"text":"स एष शाश्वतो देवः सर्वगुह्यमयः शिवः ।\nवासुदेव इति ज्ञेयो यन्मां पृच्छसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the eternal god, made of all secrets, the auspicious one; he is to be known as Vasudeva, as you ask me, Bharata."}},{"n":38,"text":"ब्राह्मणैः क्षत्रियैर्वैश्यैः शूद्रैश्च कृतलक्षणैः ।\nसेव्यतेऽभ्यर्च्यते चैव नित्ययुक्तैः स्वकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is served and worshipped by brahmins, kshatriyas, vaishyas and shudras, bearing their marks, ever devoted to their own duties."}},{"n":39,"text":"द्वापरस्य युगस्यान्ते आदौ कलियुगस्य च ।\nसात्वतं विधिमास्थाय गीतः संकर्षणेन यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the Dvapara age and the beginning of the Kali age, by the Satvata rite he was sung by Sankarshana."}},{"n":40,"text":"स एष सर्वासुरमर्त्यलोकं\nसमुद्रकक्ष्यान्तरिताः पुरीश्च ।\nयुगे युगे मानुषं चैव वासं\nपुनः पुनः सृजते वासुदेवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This same Vasudeva creates again and again, age after age, the world of asuras and mortals, the cities hidden within the sea's girdle, and his own dwelling among men."}}]}]}